Closing clears Work State and sets Lifecycle to done. For Backend Items,
it queues a Mutation; run
.B tk sync
to deliver it. tk has no command to reopen done work.
.PP
A Closing Reason must be non-empty. It is a Local Field shown by
.B tk show
and is never sent to the Backend. It can only be set when the Item closes.
Closing an already done Item without a reason is a harmless no-op;
supplying a reason then is refused.
